# Sensitive paths for shipping-work's Step 1.5 doc spot-check (#281).
# One path per line; `#`-comments and blank lines ignored. This file REPLACES
# doc-check.sh's built-in defaults rather than extending them.
#
# Entries match whole path SEGMENTS at any depth (gregoryfoster/skills#252), so
# a directory entry also flags every same-named directory elsewhere in the
# tree. Here that means the mirrored test trees, and every such over-match is
# kept deliberately — do not narrow them:
#   deploy/   -> tests/deploy/   (asserts the installed unit and the unit-only
#                                 notifier credential — DEPLOYMENT/ENVIRONMENT)
#   scripts/  -> tests/scripts/  (and the vendored skill symlinks under
#                                 skills/*/scripts/ — COMMANDS.md)
#   tools/    -> tests/tools/    (ARCHITECTURE.md's module table)
# For a spot-check that exits 1 and asks a human to look, over-matching is the
# cheap failure; the miss that exits 0 is the expensive one. Narrowing any of
# them means listing files individually, which is the under-match #252 fixed.
# tests/test_doc_sensitive_paths.py fails an entry that reaches outside its own
# tree without being named here, so this list cannot go quietly incomplete —
# it already did so twice (CR-5, CR-11).
#
# Dropped from the defaults because nothing in this repo matches them —
# a dead entry reads as coverage of a tree we do not have:
#   schema.sql     — no raw-SQL schema; Alembic owns the schema
#   src/models/    — models live under src/core/models/, covered by src/core/
#   .env.example   — env files are never committed (tests/test_env_files_are_not_committable.py)
#
# Guarded by tests/test_doc_sensitive_paths.py.

